  - `:color` - Color of the marks – either fill or stroke color based on mark type.By default, `color` represents fill color for `"area"`, `"bar"`, `"tick"`,`"text"`, `"circle"`, and `"square"` / stroke color for `"line"` and `"point"`.__Default value:__ If undefined, the default color depends on [markconfig](config.html#mark)'s `color` property._Note:_ See the scale documentation for more information about customizing [colorscheme](scale.html#scheme).
  - `:column` - Horizontal facets for trellis plots.
  - `:detail` - Additional levels of detail for grouping data in aggregate views andin line and area marks without mapping data to a specific visual channel.
  - `:href` - A URL to load upon mouse click.
  - `:opacity` - Opacity of the marks – either can be a value or a range.__Default value:__ If undefined, the default opacity depends on [markconfig](config.html#mark)'s `opacity` property.
  - `:order` - Stack order for stacked marks or order of data points in line marks for connected scatterplots.__Note__: In aggregate plots, `order` field should be `aggregate`d to avoid creatingadditional aggregation grouping.
